+@dataclass(frozen=True)
+class FrozenTopRun:
+    """ONE interval over which the AS-OF top of book `(bid, ask)` for one pair did not change.
+
+    **This is a DIFFERENT QUANTITY from `read_capture`'s `stale_runs`, and the two are never
+    merged (run-51 BLOCKER 1 + BLOCKER 3).** `stale_runs` measures "seconds the recorder's timer
+    echoed an unchanged top" — it runs `(first repeat frame, LAST repeat frame)`, needs `n > 1`,
+    and is gated on the capture declaring an emission policy, because attributing a repeat to our
+    own timer needs a declared timer to attribute it to. It feeds `_pair_coverage(stale_spans=...)`
+    -> `covered_s` / `stale_book_s` (FROZEN-MID BOOK TIME) and nothing else.
+
+    THIS quantity is the 2b detector's: the interval over which the top a trade would be priced
+    against did not change. Three consequences follow, and each was a shipped defect:
+
+      * `end_ts` is the receipt ts of the FIRST BOOK FRAME WHOSE `(bid, ask)` DIFFERS — the frame
+        that ended the run — not the last frame that repeated the top. The book stays frozen until
+        that frame arrives, so every print in the trailing keepalive window walks through the same
+        frozen book; closing at the last repeat left them outside the span (measured: moving ONE
+        print 5s later took a published 1m mean from -0.00 bp to +106.63 bp at rc=0).
+        `last_repeat_ts` keeps `stale_runs`' endpoint for disclosure so the two are comparable.
+      * A run still open at end of file ends at the capture's own `end_ts` and says so
+        (`open_at_capture_end`), rather than being closed at whatever frame happened to be last.
+      * `n >= 1`. A single frame followed by silence IS a frozen top: on a venue with no keepalive
+        it is the ONLY shape a frozen top can take, and on a declaring capture it is exactly the
+        silence interval D77-amend gates. Requiring `n > 1` here would deny the detector the shape
+        it most needs to see.
+
+    Qualifying condition: `end_ts - start_ts > STALE_BOOK_MIN_RUN_S`. Built from the record ALONE
+    and NOT gated on the emission declaration — the same reasoning `echo_runs` already applies:
+    "this top did not change between these two frames" is observable without a declaration to
+    interpret it, and an undeclared capture switching the whole 2b detector off returned the
+    original 8000 bp leak with `flagged runs {}` at rc=0.
+    """
+    start_ts: float
+    end_ts: float
+    last_repeat_ts: float
+    n: int
+    open_at_capture_end: bool
+
