+def test_the_B1_shipped_overrun_disclosure_keeps_its_EXACT_B1_semantics(tmp_path):
+    """RED against cycle 1 (which returned 1 / 102.0 here): `book_keepalive_overruns` and
+    `book_keepalive_max_interval_s` are B1-SHIPPED and RENDERED fields (the cadence-FLOOR block's
+    `BOOK KEEPALIVE OVERRUN` line). Cycle 1 REDEFINED them in place — "any recorded-gap overlap
+    exonerates" instead of "interval minus gap time still over the floor" — which silently deleted
+    the disclosure for every PARTIALLY-explained silence. A B1-shipped rendered field is never
+    redefined; the stricter variant is additive (next test).
+
+    Both intervals must count under B1 semantics: [1000 -> 1308] (308s, only 61.53s of it
+    explained, 246.47s residual > the 10s floor) and [2000 -> 2100] (102s, nothing explains it).
